times \\frac{3}{11} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{3}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{3}{11}=\\frac{1\\times 3}{2\\times 11}=\\frac{3}{22}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430670 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147407 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bee7ebc5-72be-53b1-86d8-27bd939a7244" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Answer Is a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e243e300-45bf-52c2-88fe-9276d26a1487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{63}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e243e300-45bf-52c2-88fe-9276d26a1487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{63}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430624} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c91f540-3897-5173-a2c1-f70bf2768153" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fceaf763-2a1c-5ef1-b51c-0b12e59864a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-211481" :question/problem "Expressed as a fraction in lowest terms, $\\frac{16}{9}\\times \\frac{1}{28}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the following multiplication problem:\n\n$$\n\\frac{16}{9}\\times \\frac{1}{28}\n$$\n\nNotice that the first fraction's numerator ($16$) and the second fraction's denominator ($28$) have a common \nfactor of $4.$ \n\nTherefore, we can simplify our problem by first swapping the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{16}{28}\\times \\frac{1}{9}\n$$\n\nNext, we reduce the first fraction to its lowest terms by dividing the numerator and denominator by $4.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16÷4}{28÷4}\\times \\frac{1}{9} & =\\frac{4}{7}\\times \\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{7}\\times \\frac{1}{9}=\\frac{4\\times 1}{7\\times 9}=\\frac{4}{63}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147404 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e0f80f6-920a-5eb0-919c-62c8ba67a2b9" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Multiplication and Division as Fraction Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4392b4d2-297d-58e6-99d9-30e766b8dfb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430573} {:answer/id #uuid "51277b96-b425-5410-a03e-8e82a4abb0ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430577} {:answer/id #uuid "b179e23b-e38a-5d02-af57-88a66d1ad94d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430609} {:answer/id #uuid "d1f791e7-4b44-55fc-8d13-57dd1f076e57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430617} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b315dd-7601-5527-8074-5bde772229b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2b315dd-7601-5527-8074-5bde772229b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430625} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cc2a5b9-840d-5539-9fe4-9cf233f6ccbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :que