on and division only, we can write an equivalent expression by swapping the $÷\\,3$ and the $÷\\,2$:\n\n$$\n(8\\,÷\\,2)\\times (6\\,÷\\,3)\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the $8÷2$ and $6÷3$ as fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{2}\\times \\frac{6}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147405 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2d79438-2593-55c1-a937-c40f8fc6db08" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Expression as an Equivalent Product of Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e75fdc9-1404-55dc-9f03-d37732c6be36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{4}\\times \\frac{5}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430569} {:answer/id #uuid "726dd0c5-7282-5b87-94e7-1fddc812a746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{2}\\times \\frac{15}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430589} {:answer/id #uuid "cdfc5e81-6ff3-57a1-955b-5225784b763c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{4}\\times \\frac{15}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430616} {:answer/id #uuid "d5186b3c-c46a-54c8-9800-cdb35eed99b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}\\times \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430618} {:answer/id #uuid "fac1f240-4057-532e-b3f1-603694966df6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}\\times \\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "726dd0c5-7282-5b87-94e7-1fddc812a746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{2}\\times \\frac{15}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430589} :answer-field/id #uuid "96e74002-4c9d-5381-9f69-a74e1f840163" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :a